    "existing_models_exempt": false,
    "results_to_customers": "numeric_rates",
    "public_publication": false,
    "quote": "Each model must undergo a sustained-heat test at 55 °C before market entry and at least annually, using a representative sample and a common test protocol agreed by the parties. A model with a failure rate above 10% must not be newly marketed. For a model with a failure rate above 5% and up to 10%, the manufacturer must implement corrective action and enhanced monitoring, and provide its corrective-action plan to regulators."
   },
